    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "Testing is complete — all 19 checklist items were executed and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 3 FAIL**\n\nThe core to-do functionality is solid: task creation with full details, editing, deletion, completion, active/completed view switching with accurate counts, priority and deadline sorting (including undated tasks placed last), empty-title validation, and cycle-free prerequisite selection all behaved correctly.\n\n**Three defects found:**\n\n1. **FT-3 — Blocked tasks are completely uneditable.** The spec requires that a blocked task still allow description and priority changes, with only title and deadline locked. In practice the edit button is `disabled=true`, and there is no alternative editing path (card click, title double-click, inline fields), so *no* field can be modified while a task is blocked.\n\n2. **CS-22 — Invalid completed-and-blocked state.** Reopening a completed prerequisite is allowed with no warning or cascade, leaving the dependent task simultaneously counted as completed (in the Completed view, line-through styling) *and* displaying its \"Prerequisite ... incomplete\" blocked warning — exactly the contradictory state the constraint forbids.\n\n3. **IX-18 — Dashed connection lines are purely decorative.** The connector renders as a bare 2×12px `<div>` whose React props contain only `className` — no hover handlers or tooltip trigger. Hovering produces no popup. The dependency-chain popup exists only on the warning badge (IX-20, which passes), not on the visual connection itself.\n\nNotably, FT-3 and IX-18 represent partial implementations of the dependency feature: the blocking *indication* works well, but the two behaviors that qualify it — restricted-field editing and the interactive connection line — are missing."
  }
}
